---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import samples from '../../data/samples.json';
const files=[{name:'Canon EOS R6 Mark II',sample:samples[0],mode:'Full-frame normal RAW (CR3)'},{name:'Sony A7 III',sample:samples[1],mode:'14-bit compressed RAW (ARW)'},{name:'Nikon D750',sample:samples[2],mode:'14-bit lossless compressed RAW (NEF)'}];
const format=(n:number)=>(n/1e6).toFixed(2);
const paths=[['/raw-file-size/','RAW file size'],['/compressed-vs-uncompressed-raw/','RAW compression'],['/raw-plus-jpeg/','RAW + JPEG']];
---
<Layout title="RAW File Size: Real Camera Measurements & Storage" description="How large is a RAW photograph? Compare three measured original camera files, learn what changes file size, and calculate memory-card capacity."><article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">FILE SIZE GUIDE</p><h1>How big is a RAW file?</h1><p class="lead">There is no single RAW file size. Resolution, bit depth, compression and the recorded scene all affect storage. Our three documented originals measure from {format(Math.min(...files.map(f=>f.sample.rawBytes)))} MB to {format(Math.max(...files.map(f=>f.sample.rawBytes)))} MB. That range describes these samples only, not all cameras.</p><h2>Measured RAW file sizes by camera</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Single original files measured in decimal megabytes; not camera averages</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Camera</th><th scope="col">Capture mode</th><th scope="col">Measured RAW</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{files.map(f=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/${f.sample.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`}>{f.name}</a></th><td>{f.mode}</td><td>{format(f.sample.rawBytes)} MB</td><td><a href={f.sample.url}>Original CC0 file ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>What determines RAW file size?</h2><p>Higher-resolution captures typically contain more sensor values. Higher bit depth may use more storage depending on packing and codec. Uncompressed files generally have more predictable sizes, whereas compressed files can change with scene content and camera processing. Cropping and some specialized capture modes also change file dimensions.</p><h2>Are CR3, ARW and NEF files the same size?</h2><p>No. These are manufacturer RAW families with different recording modes and internal layouts. A file extension alone does not tell you how many megabytes a photograph will occupy. Compare files from matching camera settings rather than estimating a Nikon NEF from a Canon CR3.</p><h2>How many RAW photographs fit on 128 GB?</h2><p>The table below divides a nominal 128,000 MB capacity by each original RAW byte count. These are planning estimates before filesystem overhead, not measured card capacities.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Camera sample</th><th>One RAW file</th><th>128 GB (theoretical)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{files.map(f=><tr><th scope="row">{f.name}</th><td>{format(f.sample.rawBytes)} MB</td><td>{Math.floor(128e9/f.sample.rawBytes).toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>Why is a JPEG usually smaller?</h2><p>JPEG is rendered and uses lossy image compression. RAW retains information intended for later development, although some cameras also compress RAW data. JPEG settings, scene detail and output resolution vary, so a fixed RAW-to-JPEG multiplier is unreliable. Our calculator's default 8 MB JPEG is an adjustable assumption, not a measured independent JPEG in this dataset.</p><h2>Measure your own files accurately</h2><p>Check the actual byte size of several original photographs from your preferred shooting mode and use a representative number. Record bit depth, crop setting, compression and ISO before comparing sizes. Keep the source files and measurement method with your results so others can reproduce them.</p></article><section class="wrap prose compact"><h2>Related guides and tools</h2><ul>{paths.map(([href,label])=><li><a href={href}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul><p><a href="/cameras/">Measured camera index</a> · <a href="/memory-card-calculator/">Memory card calculator</a> · <a href="/methodology/">Sources and methods</a> · <a href="/">Compare RAW and JPEG</a></p></section></Layout>